Goldenland: AI Assist low-credit gate removed — decided in a /grilling design session. Balance now drives warnings only (never blocks); warnings on both AI Settings and generation UI; `openrouter_minimum_balance` ($1) kept as warning threshold; 402 is fallback-eligible so [paid, free] chains degrade to free; free models work at $0 balance; chain remains the single admin decision point ('Global model chain'). Captured in ADR 0009 and CONTEXT.md. Implemented: `OpenRouterFailureClassifier` marks credit failures fallback-eligible; `OpenRouterHealthService::catalog()` serves catalog without hitting credit endpoint (seam moved from `check()` to `catalog()`); providers use `catalog()`; settings page and edit pages show warning banners on low/stale balance; helper text documents fallback. Added shared health fakes `contentHealthFake`/`observationHealth` across provider test files; updated tests (402 now fallback-eligible in classifier and client tests). <!-- created=2026-08-08, last=2026-08-08 -->
