goldenland-realestate-v2: tests run on SQLite, which masks MySQL-only migration failures (after() column order and the 3072-byte InnoDB key limit on utf8mb4 indexes are not enforced by SQLite). The MySQL dev DB (goldenland_realestate_v2 via Herd) was behind on migrations and had drifted tables (e.g. a hand-created empty keyword_observations with no migration record). Fixed in commits 072aa91 + e3e07a6: two out-of-order after() clauses dropped; keyword_observations/ga4_landing_page_observations 5-column unique indexes fixed by constraining source(64), site_url(191), event_name(64). If a migration suddenly fails on MySQL but passes tests, check for these two patterns first. Also: dev OpenRouter account balance went negative (-$0.10) from earlier paid test runs; negative balance 402s ALL requests including :free models until topped up (ADR 0009). <!-- created=2026-08-08, last=2026-08-08 -->
